  // Stump check: cut the oak at (-79, 14, -2) (see trees.json for how it was found; its root and the
  // three cells over it are a full 16 px log) at its third cell, so the root stays as a stump and the
  // cell between it and the cut goes with the fell. Run from OpenGLTest/ with
  //   VOXEL_TIME=147 VOXEL_SCRIPT=visual-examples/stump.json
  // Look for a stump five pixels high with a flared base where the root stood, no log left between
  // it and the ground, and the rest of the tree on the ground. Then an oak log is stood on the stump with a
  // right-click (log_placed), wobbled by a left-click (log_wobble, shot 0.1 s after the blow) and lifted off with a
  // second right-click (log_taken: the stump bare again). Last the log goes back on and an axe splits it: a slow
  // overhead swing (axe_swing, 0.5 s in; the swing only advances while a `mine` step holds the click, as the real
  // game's per-frame input does), then wood chips and sixteen lumber on the ground (split_after).
